        "original_id": "5804a860-4628-5ea2-a7d1-d238499f124e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Gordonia, Osbeckia, Franklinia, Camellia, Stewartia\n- Places: Gordonia-Alatamaha State Park, Altamaha River\n- Concepts: plant genera, plant families, park naming\n\nFacts:\n- Gordonia is a genus of flowering plants in the family Theaceae.\n- Gordonia is related to Franklinia, Camellia, and Stewartia.\n- Osbeckia is a genus of plants in the family Melastomataceae.\n- Gordonia-Alatamaha State Park is named for the nearby Altamaha River.\n- Gordonia-Alatamaha State Park is also named for the park's nearly extinct Gordonia tree.",
